patch type="fixed" "The signalling URL is no longer logged with the access token in it. On web the token is carried as a query parameter, because browsers cannot set headers on a WebSocket, and the whole URL was logged at FINE level — so an app that enabled FINE logging, or forwarded SDK logs, wrote a usable access token to its logs. The token is now masked in that log line, matching the JS SDK; the remaining query parameters are still logged"
